  "summary": "Several studies directly apply transformer-based architectures, specifically self-attention encoder models, to the task of estimating agricultural yield. Chen et al. (2020) utilize self-attention encoder models on the AgriSat-4 dataset, achieving an accuracy of 0.88 [V0029]. Similarly, El-Sayed et al. (2022) apply self-attention encoder models to the CellLife dataset, reporting an AUROC of 0.67 [V0031]. Fischer et al. (2023) evaluate self-attention encoder models on ToxiBench, obtaining an F1 score of 0.74 [V0032]. Duarte et al. (2021) deploy self-attention encoder models on LedgerGuard, reporting a Mean Absolute Error (MAE) of 0.6 [V0030]. For comparison, a non-transformer approach by Haddad et al. (2025) uses boosted decision-tree ensembles on ToxiBench with an MAE of 0.61 [V0040].",
